  "declared_proposition": "For f(x)=L^(-1) sum_k F_k exp(2*pi*i*k*x/L), define cyclic spectral autocorrelation C_h=sum_k F_(k+h) conjugate(F_k). Then |f(x)|^2=L^(-2) sum_h C_h exp(2*pi*i*h*x/L), and therefore ||f||_infinity <= sqrt(sum_h |C_h|)/L. This certificate retains relative phase. The diagonal energy C_0 alone cannot control the uniform norm: a single coefficient sqrt(L) and L aligned unit coefficients both have C_0=L, but their uniform norms are L^(-1/2) and 1.",
